    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Kill Devil Hills grew into a tourist beach town after the Wright Brothers' 1903 flights, earning national fame.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.killdevilhills.com/history.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town's name origin theories involve pirates and rum barrels strong enough to \"kill the devil\".",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.killdevilhills.com/history.html",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1903, Wilbur and Orville Wright made four powered flights at the base of the big hill now part of the national monument.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kdhnc.com/58/ResidentsBusinesses",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Kill Devil Hills Life Saving Station, established in 1878, was one of eleven lifesaving stations along the Outer Banks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.killdevilhills.com/history.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Sam's Diner, listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1999, sits beside the Wright Brothers National Memorial.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
